  "notes": "Page numbers are PDF page = printed page. Pin table Table 3-1 p11. 3V3 abs max -0.3..3.6 V (Table 6-1 p21, symbol VDD33), rec 3.0..3.6 V typ 3.3 (Table 6-2 p21); external supply must deliver >= 0.5 A (IVDD, p21). Pin names as printed: IO18 = GPIO18/USB_D-, IO19 = GPIO19/USB_D+, RXD0 = GPIO20/U0RXD (pad 30), TXD0 = GPIO21/U0TXD (pad 31); pin-type column is I/O/T for all IOs. Pin 3 is the only 3V3 pad. GND pads: 1,2,11,14,36-53 (53 = central thermal/GND pad group per Fig 3-1 p10; 49 is also center GND). NC pads: 4,7,9,10,15,17,24,25,28,29,32-35. Datasheet: 'Do not leave the EN pin floating' (p11); EN high=on, low=off; VIH_nRST 0.75*VDD, VIL_nRST 0.25*VDD (p21-22). STRAPPING (Section 4, p12-13): GPIO2 (pad 5, IO2), GPIO8 (pad 22, IO8), GPIO9 (pad 23, IO9). Defaults Table 4-1 p12: GPIO2 floating, GPIO8 floating, GPIO9 weak pull-up (1). Boot mode Table 4-3 p13: SPI boot = GPIO2 1, GPIO8 any, GPIO9 1; Joint download boot (USB-Serial-JTAG / UART download) = GPIO2 1, GPIO8 1, GPIO9 0. Footnote p13: GPIO2 does not actually determine these modes but pulling it up is recommended due to glitches. GPIO8 also controls ROM message printing (p12, Table 4-4 p14 not read). Strapping timing: tSU min 0 ms, tH min 3 ms (Table 4-2 p13). Datasheet also says 'the strapping pin mapping between the chip and modules: see Chapter 8' (schematics, not read). Variant note: H4X = ESP32-C3FH4X chip variant per datasheet series; module ordering table p3-4 not read for this suffix. Pin 53 center-pad assignment: Fig 3-1 shows pads 49-53 as GND, consistent with the Table 3-1 range 36-53.",
